        "original_id": "0a0c2db5-6847-56a7-a839-ddcbb08b17e1",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Paul Newman, Robert Redford, Robert Shaw\n- Characters: Doc Hudson\n- Films: Cars, Cars 3, The Sting\n- Companies: Disney-Pixar, Pixar\n- Topics: voice acting, posthumous credits, animated characters, caper films\n\nFacts:\n- The Sting is a 1973 American caper film set in September 1936.\n- The Sting involves two professional grifters played by Paul Newman and Robert Redford who con a mob boss played by Robert Shaw.\n- Doc Hudson is an animated anthropomorphic retired race car who appears in the 2006 Pixar film Cars.\n- In Cars, Doc Hudson serves as a medical doctor and a local judge.\n- Paul Newman voiced Doc Hudson in the first Cars film produced by Disney-Pixar.\n- Paul Newman received a posthumous credit for his voice recordings in Cars 3, which was released in 2017.",
